<% content_for :head do %>
  <% set_meta_tags(
    title: "B2B SaaS Development Company",
    description: "We build, rescue and scale multi-tenant SaaS platforms, and add AI features to products that already have customers. Milestone delivery, you own the code.",
    keywords: "B2B SaaS development partner, SaaS platform engineering, B2B SaaS development company, multi-tenant SaaS, platform modernization, AI features for SaaS"
  ) %>
  <script type="application/ld+json">
  <%= raw({
    "@context" => "https://schema.org",
    "@type" => "Service",
    "name" => "B2B SaaS Development and Modernization",
    "url" => industry_b2b_saas_url,
    "description" => "We build, rescue and scale multi-tenant SaaS platforms, and add AI features to products that already have customers.",
    "provider" => { "@id" => "https://astechware.com/#organization" },
    "areaServed" => ["United States", "United Kingdom", "Canada", "Australia"],
    "serviceType" => "B2B SaaS Engineering",
    "category" => "B2B SaaS"
  }.to_json) %>
  </script>
<% end %>

<div class="hero-section py-5 service-page-hero b2b-saas-hero industry-landing-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row align-items-center min-vh-50">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-9 mx-auto text-center">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3" style="font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 56px); line-height: 1.2;" data-page-h1>
          B2B SaaS development and modernization
        </h1>
        <p class="text-white fw-semibold mb-3" style="font-size: clamp(18px, 2.5vw, 22px); line-height: 1.4; max-width: 720px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
          Full Platform Builds, AI Growth Engines, and Infrastructure Modernization
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4" style="font-size: clamp(16px, 2vw, 18px); line-height: 1.6; max-width: 800px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.95);">
          We build, rescue and scale multi-tenant SaaS platforms, and add AI features to products that already have customers. Milestone delivery, you own the code.
        </p>
        <a href="https://calendly.com/ahmadkamran/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg rounded-pill px-5">
          Book a 30-min call
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="inner-sections b2b-saas-industry-page">

  <section class="py-5 bg-white" id="what-we-do">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
          <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">What we actually do</h2>
          <p class="large-para mb-4">
            Most SaaS work we take on is not a greenfield pitch deck. It is a product that already has customers, a search that times out, a monolith that cannot ship weekly, or a team that wants AI without breaking what works.
          </p>
          <p class="large-para mb-5">
            We focus on three kinds of engagements where we have shipped production systems:
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="row g-4">
        <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 p-lg-5 h-100">
            <h3 class="h5 mb-3">Rescue and stabilize</h3>
            <p class="mb-0 small" style="line-height: 1.7;">
              Performance audits, search rebuilds, queue hardening, and foundation fixes when the platform is crashing or cart abandonment is driven by slow lookups.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 p-lg-5 h-100">
            <h3 class="h5 mb-3">Modernize without downtime</h3>
            <p class="mb-0 small" style="line-height: 1.7;">
              Strangler Fig migrations from legacy stacks to headless React/Node (or equivalent), with incremental cutovers so the business keeps running.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 p-lg-5 h-100">
            <h3 class="h5 mb-3">Add AI to products that already ship</h3>
            <p class="mb-0 small" style="line-height: 1.7;">
              Marketing workflows, content generation, and automation layered onto existing product data, with guardrails and explainability, not a rewrite for its own sake.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 p-lg-5 h-100">
            <h3 class="h5 mb-3">First multi-tenant product builds</h3>
            <p class="mb-0 small" style="line-height: 1.7;">
              Founders building the first real multi-tenant SaaS: isolation, billing hooks, admin surfaces, and a codebase they own from day one.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-light-grey" id="spotlights">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="text-center mb-5">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-3 pb-3 d-inline-block">Case studies</h2>
        <p class="text-muted mb-0">Rescue, modernization, and AI features on live products.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="row g-4">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-4">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 p-lg-5 h-100">
            <h3 class="h5 mb-3">Restaurant resource: search and stability rescue</h3>
            <p class="mb-0" style="line-height: 1.7;">
              Emergency performance audit for a B2B supplier catalog. Replaced broken SQL LIKE search with Meilisearch, stabilized Sidekiq, and rebuilt ingestion for real time inventory updates.
            </p>
            <%= link_to "Read the full case study &rarr;".html_safe, case_study_path("restaurant-resource-rescue"), class: "d-inline-block mt-4 fw-semibold ajax" %>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-4">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 p-lg-5 h-100">
            <h3 class="h5 mb-3">Word of mouth: modernization with no downtime</h3>
            <p class="mb-0" style="line-height: 1.7;">
              Live heart transplant of a national marketplace from legacy PHP/jQuery to a headless React/Node stack using the Strangler Fig pattern, with continuous cutovers and business continuity.
            </p>
            <%= link_to "Read the full case study &rarr;".html_safe, case_study_path("word-of-mouth-modernization"), class: "d-inline-block mt-4 fw-semibold ajax" %>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-4">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 p-lg-5 h-100">
            <h3 class="h5 mb-3">EventVesta: AI marketing workflows</h3>
            <p class="mb-0" style="line-height: 1.7;">
              Modernized a legacy events UI to React and built an AI marketing workflow: generate posts and ad creative, schedule to Meta, generate Meta and Google campaigns, with guardrails and explainable reports.
            </p>
            <%= link_to "Read the full case study &rarr;".html_safe, case_study_path("eventvesta-ai-marketing"), class: "d-inline-block mt-4 fw-semibold ajax" %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-white" id="who-we-work-with">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
          <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">Who we work with</h2>
          <ul class="mb-0 ps-3 large-para" style="line-height: 2;">
            <li>SaaS products that have hit their limits on search, stability, or release cadence</li>
            <li>SaaS teams adding AI features to products that already have customers</li>
            <li>Founders building their first multi-tenant product</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-light-grey" id="engage">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
          <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">How we engage</h2>
          <p class="large-para mb-4">
            We start with a paid one week scoping call. You get a written deliverable you own whether or not you continue with us:
          </p>
          <div class="workflow-card p-4 p-lg-5 mb-4">
            <ul class="mb-0 ps-3" style="line-height: 2;">
              <li>A map of your current architecture, bottlenecks, and tenant boundaries</li>
              <li>A risk register covering stability, data isolation, and migration cutover risk</li>
              <li>An architecture recommendation with build vs rescue sequencing</li>
              <li>A phased plan with milestones</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="text-center">
            <a href="https://calendly.com/ahmadkamran/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg rounded-pill px-5">
              Book a 30-min call
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-white" id="faq">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="text-center mb-5">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-3 pb-3 d-inline-block">FAQ</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
          <div class="accordion b2b-saas-industry-faq" id="b2bSaasIndustryFaq">
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#saasfaq1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="saasfaq1">Can you modernize a live product without downtime?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="saasfaq1" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#b2bSaasIndustryFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">Yes. We use incremental patterns (Strangler Fig, gateway routing, dual running) so traffic moves in stages. Word of Mouth was a live marketplace modernization with continuous cutovers, not a big bang rewrite.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#saasfaq2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="saasfaq2">Do you build AI features into existing SaaS products?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="saasfaq2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#b2bSaasIndustryFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">Yes. EventVesta is an example: React modernization plus AI content and ad workflows on top of existing event data, with guardrails and explainability. We prefer AI that sits on real product data over greenfield &ldquo;AI products&rdquo; with no users.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#saasfaq3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="saasfaq3">Who owns the code?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="saasfaq3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#b2bSaasIndustryFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">You do. Milestone delivery, repositories in your accounts, no lock in. Retainer support is optional after launch.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-2">
              <h3 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#saasfaq4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="saasfaq4">What if we only need a rescue, not a rebuild?</button>
              </h3>
              <div id="saasfaq4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#b2bSaasIndustryFaq">
                <div class="accordion-body">That is often the right starting point. Restaurant Resource began as an emergency performance and search rescue. Stabilize first, then decide what to modernize.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%= render "shared/hire_cta" %>

</div>
